Pre-existing-corruption repair (TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj):
  This branch's TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj was committed corrupt (HEAD 8804add5f): TWO concatenated <Project>
  roots (lines 1-893 + 894-1682) plus several malformed comment/ItemGroup boundaries that failed XML load with
  MSB4025, so `dotnet build`/`dotnet test` could not even load the project (a pre-existing integration-branch
  defect, NOT introduced here; a prior agent left a note about the same MSB4025 class at the DrivingPerformanceCards
  block). Repaired deterministically: dropped the duplicate <Project> root, removed the broken boundaries, and
  consolidated every linked source into well-formed ItemGroups (deduplicated to avoid NETSDK1022), preserving all
  364 previously-linked sources -- including the ChargingTab triple, which had only survived in the discarded
  duplicate root (so the repair also RESTORES ChargingTab's headless test coverage) -- and adding the TitleSlide
  link. Verified: the csproj now loads as XML with a single root, the whole solution builds, and 8091 tests pass.

Web source parity (web/src/features/analytics/components/review/TitleSlide.tsx):
  States reproduced: Content (car emoji + count-up year + t('yearReview.title','Year in Review') + vehicle name)
    and Empty (emoji over the title + t('yearReview.noDriveData','No drive data for this year'), never a blank box).
    The web source is purely presentational (single prop data: YearReview; hook useTranslation only) with no
    conditional branch, so there is no fetch-driven loading/error/stale/offline branch to reproduce in the slide --
    the parent year-in-review story page owns those, exactly as the DriveHighlightSlide/AuditPanel/ResultPanel ports
    document. The Empty branch is the native robustness path for the absent/sentinel model (never-blank rule).
  Data sources mapped: useTranslation -> ILocalizer facade (no HTTP in the view; model is supplied by the parent).
  Shared components mapped: @/components/data-display AnimatedNumber -> TsAnimatedNumber (count-up, en-US grouping,
    reduce-motion aware) scaled to a hero size via a height-locked Viewbox; @/components/motion (framer-motion
    staggered entrance) -> TsStaggerContainer (OS reduce-motion aware); typography -> tokenized DisplayTokens
    brushes (TextSecondary; no raw hex).
  Year formatting: web fmtNumber/toLocaleString grouping (2026 -> "2,026") reproduced via NumberFormatting.Format,
    matching what the TsAnimatedNumber count-up shows on screen.
  i18n: yearReview.title + yearReview.noDriveData resolve through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade and are present in
    the shared catalog ("Year in Review" / "No drive data for this year"); no English literals beyond the fallbacks
    the web t() also passes.
  Accessibility: surface Narrator name in both states (year, title, vehicle -- or the title + empty message);
    decorative emoji and the count-up wrapper are AccessibilityView.Raw; the empty state is a live region;
    TextBlocks honour the system font scale; the entrance honours OS reduce-motion via TsStaggerContainer.
  Telemetry: TitleSlideDiagnostics emits "view.opened slug=TitleSlide" (PII-safe; never the year or vehicle name)
    on first load.

